      "title": "Dilution",
      "excerpt": "DILUTION The\ndifference between the public offering price per unit and the net tangible book value (NTBV) per Class\u00a0A ordinary share after this\noffering constitutes the dilution to investors in this offering. NTBV per share is determined by dividing our NTBV, which is our total\ntangible assets less total liabilities, by the number of outstanding Class\u00a0A ordinary shares. The below calculations (A)\u00a0assume that (i)\u00a0no ordinary\nshares are issued to shareholders of a potential business combination target as consideration or issuable by a post-business combination\ncompany, for instance under an equity or employee share purchase plan, (ii)\u00a0no ordinary shares and convertible equity or debt securities\nare issued in connection with additional financing that we may seek in connection with an initial business combination, (iii)\u00a0no\nworking capital loans are converted into private placement units, as ",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    }
  ],
